  "label": "The man in the mugshot is mapped as the subject of the 'stand your ground law' text.",
  "description": "The top text 'stand your ground law.' is juxtaposed with the visual of the man in a mugshot pose, implying that the man is the subject or embodiment of this legal concept. The visual material (the man) is being mapped onto the textual material (the law) to create a satirical association, suggesting the man is 'standing his ground' under the law, despite the absurd and racially charged context provided by the bottom text.",
